WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.538
[MUSIC]

00:00:06.538 --> 00:00:11.513
Folks who take a growth mindset,
see the challenges they're

00:00:11.513 --> 00:00:16.680
facing as something that they
could develop enough to achieve or

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.070
overcome or master or learn from.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:25.820
So that a failure from a growth mindset
perspective is an opportunity to learn.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:30.610
One of the things that goes on when you
are learning in the context of a number of

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.900
other people who are different from you,

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:37.199
you're confronted with experiences
that you would never have had.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.200
Now, if you're in a group with
a lot of people who look and

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.320
have very different experiences.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.750
And now you begin to share those
experiences, you gain from that

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:52.590
living knowledge about what it's
like to be a very different person.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:56.300
And they're saying, well, here's what
happened when we used that approach.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.170
And somebody else will raise
their hand and say, yeah, but

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:02.330
here's what happened when we use that
approach, and they're so different.

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:06.770
And that's incredibly educational
from a developmental perspective.

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:11.270
It makes you begin to realize things that
you have been taking for granted, or

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.470
possibilities that
you've never considered.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:18.500
I remember hearing a Ukrainian
mass retailer comparing what

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:23.590
was going on in his organization,
to an executive from Lululemon.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:26.710
And the learning that came out
of that interaction was amazing,

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:30.200
that diversity allows you to
start thinking of possibilities.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.031
And remember, it's thinking of
possibilities that makes it possible for

00:01:34.031 --> 00:01:36.726
us to engage in the developmental
approach to work.

00:01:36.726 --> 00:01:39.066
[MUSIC]

00:01:39.066 --> 00:01:43.870
&gt;&gt; Question your assumptions and
explore new approaches to leadership.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.523
Explore Stanford's upcoming programs.

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:52.012
[MUSIC]

